OL,3,CIn pictures: When the world plunged
OL,4,Cinto darkness in the 1999 solar eclipse
OL,6,FIn 1999, ITV News reporter Norman Rees
OL,7,Fjoined the hundreds of thousands of
OL,8,Fpeople who gathered in Cornwall to
OL,9,Fwatch the solar eclipse
OL,11,FOn Wednesday evening, skygazers in the
OL,12,FUK, and Europe will be treated to its
OL,13,Ffullest solar eclipse since 1999.
OL,15,FThe Moon will pass between the Sun and
OL,16,Fthe Earth between 6pm and 8pm, and
OL,17,Fbriefly all three celestial bodies
OL,18,Fwill be aligned.
OL,20,FUp to 96% of the Sun could be obscured
OL,21,Fin parts of the country.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G1/6
