OL,3,CIn pictures: When the world plunged
OL,4,Cinto darkness in the 1999 solar eclipse
OL,6,FPeople came up with creative ways to
OL,7,Fview the eclipse, sticking eclipse
OL,8,Fglasses to the end of cameras to
OL,9,Fcapture the moment.
OL,11,FThe peak of this year's solar eclipse
OL,12,Fwill be between 7.05pm and 7.16pm.
OL,14,FThe UK Health Security Agency strongly
OL,15,Fadvises people not to look directly
OL,16,Finto the Sun without safe, industry-
OL,17,Fstandard eclipse glasses, as this can
OL,18,Fseriously damage the eyes.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G5/6
